     "span": "बाहरी गुण के अभिमान से",
     "evidence": "Tibetan 'ཕྱིར་ལ་ཡོན་ཏན་རློམ་པ་ཡིས' (Skt 'अपरं गुणमानेन'): ཕྱིར་ལ is the adverbial 'moreover/furthermore' (English: 'Moreover, conceited about his good qualities'). bo-kunpal 8-145 glosses it as conceit about qualities he does not have ('ཡོན་ཏན་མེད་བཞིན་དུ་ཡོན་ཏན་ཅན་དུ་རློམས་པ'). Nothing in the Tibetan says the qualities are 'outer/external' (बाहरी); the Hindi read ཕྱིར་ as 'outside' and added a qualifier.",
